720$ K","$640$ K"],"answer":0,"solution":"From the unit of the rate constant (s$^{-1}$), the reaction is of first order.<br><br>The rate constant at temperature $T_2$ is:<br><br>$k_2 = \\dfrac{0.693}{t_{1/2}} = \\dfrac{0.693}{152} \\approx 4.56 \\times 10^{-3}$ s$^{-1}$<br><br>Using the Arrhenius equation:<br><br>$\\log \\left( \\dfrac{k_2}{k_1} \\right) = \\dfrac{E_a}{2.303 R} \\left( \\dfrac{1}{T_1} - \\dfrac{1}{T_2} \\right)$<br><br>Substituting the given values:<br><br>$\\dfrac{E_a}{2.303 R} = \\dfrac{191.47 \\times 10^3}{2.303 \\times 8.314} = \\dfrac{191470}{19.147} = 10000$ K<br><br>$\\log \\left( \\dfrac{4.56 \\times 10^{-3}}{5.0 \\times 10^{-5}} \\right) = 10000 \\left( \\dfrac{1}{600} - \\dfrac{1}{T_2} \\right)$<br><br>$\\log (91.2) = 10000 \\left( \\dfrac{1}{600} - \\dfrac{1}{T_2} \\right)$<br><br>$1.96 = 10000 \\left( \\dfrac{1}{600} - \\dfrac{1}{T_2} \\right)$<br><br>$\\dfrac{1}{600} - \\dfrac{1}{T_2} = 0.000196$<br><br>$\\dfrac{1}{T_2} = \\dfrac{1}{600} - 0.000196 = 0.001667 - 0.000196 = 0.001471$ K$^{-1}$<br><br>$T_2 = \\dfrac{1}{0.001471} \\approx 680$ K<br><br>Answer: $680$ K","difficulty":"Hard","source":"IAT (IISER) 2026","_marksId":"6a4521848c20d3b91d64f970"},{"id":23993,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemical Kinetics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"Which of the following statements is INCORRECT?","options":["Half-life of a first order reaction is independent of the initial concentration of reactant.","Half-life of a zero order reaction is proportional to the rate constant.","Half-life of a first order reaction is inversely proportional to the rate constant.","Half-life of a zero order reaction is proportional to the initial concentration of reactant."],"answer":1,"solution":"No solution available. ","difficulty":"Medium","source":"IAT (IISER) 2021","_marksId":"67fdff62378e1624ea7b6adb"},{"id":23994,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemical Kinetics","exam":"Engineering","examName":"IAT (IISER)","q":"A first-order reaction 